[PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]
## Consolidated Experience from Similar Tasks
Consolidated lessons for object placement and manipulation: (1) For a put-down task, first locate the object, pick it up, then locate a valid target surface; if the named target instance is unavailable, explore other instances or retry instead of stopping. (2) Before attempting pick_up, ensure the robot hand is empty; if holding another object, place/drop it first. (3) Path planning matters: before moving toward a target, check that the intended path is clear and route around obstacles rather than assuming forward motion will succeed. (4) Do not infer that an object is unreachable solely because movement is blocked; check the object's actual proximity to the robot before predicting pickup failure. (5) When find fails, do not assume the target is absent or invisible; explore the environment, check alternate locations, or confirm availability. (6) Success is indicated by successful find and pick_up of the object, successful find of a valid target surface, and a successful final put_down.

## Preliminary Thinking
1. Verify the robot hand is empty; if not, place or drop the held object. 2. Search for the newspaper. If find fails, explore alternate locations or retry rather than concluding it is absent. 3. Plan a clear route to the newspaper: check for obstacles before moving, navigate around any blockage, and adjust if Move fails. 4. Attempt pick_up once close enough; if it fails, check hand state and actual object proximity rather than assuming obstruction means unreachable. 5. Search for the couch. If the specific couch instance is unavailable, explore other couch instances or valid target surfaces. 6. Plan a clear route to the couch, avoiding obstacles. 7. Execute put_down to place the newspaper on the couch. 8. Confirm success by checking find/pick_up for the newspaper, find for the target surface, and put_down completion.
[/PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]